    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0829" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg695"/>

                <head>No. 504.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Phelps.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 31,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phelps</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister London:</hi></p>
                <p>It is reported by the United States consul-general at Halifax that two American
                    fishing vessels have put into that port for repairs, with cargoes of fresh fish
                    on board, and that the Canadian authorities have forbidden the sale of the fish
                    as being in violation of treaty and British statutes. A persistent refusal will
                    necessitate throwing the fish overboard. <pb facs="0830" n="696" xml:id="pg696"
                    /> Will not this violation of international law and comity be proven ted by
                    Great Britain pending our sincere efforts to effect a friendly settlement?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
